active coordinate `z`, the source/output exponents are respectively `z⁻¹`
and `(a + z)⁻¹`.  A standard homogeneous hard-amplitude split would need the
same power rate for the two endpoint tails.  The following calculation shows
that the two chord rates are strictly different whenever the active endpoint
is genuinely moved.
